Hogwarts Legacy has not shied away at  all from the Dark Side of magic in the  Wizarding World if anything it appears  dark magic will be featured quite  prominently in the game given how much  attention the Avalanche marketing team  has devoted to it the original Harry  Potter series was known for its twists  and having characters take surprising  turns from Severus Snape and his role as  a double agent to Remus Lupine and his  true identity as a werewolf to Sirius  Black who ended up being Harry's  Godfather after we first thought him a  murderer an ultimate traitor to Harry's  parents we've been introduced to a  handful of Hogwarts Legacy characters so  far but which ones could actually end up  surprising us and be evil here are five  characters who could turn out to be evil  in Hogwarts Legacy we'll start with  Professor eliezar fig who's described as  both our friend and Mentor in a Hogwarts  Legacy Playstation blog post we also  know he's been investigating rumors of a  goblin Rebellion which doesn't sit well  with the ministry of magic at the time  having a mentor turn out to be a foe is  a familiar Trope and one we've seen even  in the Potter series before one of the  most notable examples happens in Harry's  fourth year at Hogwarts with Professor  moody or fake Moody that is in Harry  Potter and the Goblet of Fire Harry  quite enjoys Moody's style of teaching  but is shocked and appalled to find out  that at the end of the book Moody has  been leading him right to Voldemort all  along and his true identity was Barty  Crouch Jr a Death Eater for Voldemort  many fans have speculated about figs  since his initial reveal but is there  anything we've seen so far to actually  back up the claims that he could be evil  well truth be told there's not a lot but  there is one head-scratching moment in  the trailer during Fig's confrontation  with the goblin ranrock the trailer  clearly wants to position ranrock as the  bad guy here but in this scene we'll  find our main character and fig  appearing to be in Gringotts they're  then confronted by ran Rock and two of  his guards but notice it's actually fig  who strikes first only after his initial  attack do we see ran Rock retaliate with  powerful magic of his own to be fair to  Fig we don't know what happened in the  lead up to this moment but I've always  found it pretty interesting that he  strike first if not fig though what  about one of the other professors such  as Professor heckett considering all the  drama that played out with the defense  against the dark arts post during Harry  Potter's day this one may be a bit too  on the nose then again the problems for  this position started thanks to a curse  from Tom Riddle when Dumbledore didn't  give him the job and yet the name heckit  is likely inspired by hecatee or hekate  the Greek goddess of magic witchcraft  the Knight Moon ghost and necromancy the  closest thing to necromancy in the Harry  Potter series comes in the form of  inferior which are animated corpses of  the dead but in theory aren't  resurrected Spirits rather they are  essentially puppets controlled by a dark  Wizard and this is the most important  Point here inferior are not naturally  occurring in The Wizarding World they  only show up under a powerful spell with  a dark wizard at the center of it of all  the witches and wizards we know about so  far in Hogwarts Legacy it's Rookwood who  probably seems like the most likely  candidate but we also can't discount  Professor heckett either of all the new  characters that have been revealed for  for Hogwarts Legacy we arguably know  more about Sebastian sallow than anyone  else at first glance Sebastian appears  to fall perfectly in line with a  stereotypical rebellious Slytherin he  appears to have a habit of breaking  rules and being somewhat of a rebel it's  even been confirmed Sebastian will lead  us down a path into Dark Magic by  offering to teach us one of the  unforgivable spells and yet he certainly  has a compelling reason for doing so his  twin sister Anne suffers from a  debilitating curse and Sebastian  believes there's a path to save her but  only with the help of dark magic so  while Sebastian may be the one teaching  us at least some form of dark magic I'm  not sure we'll ever see him as a truly  evil or malicious character in the game  in fact his story gives me hope that  Hogwarts Legacy will feature plenty of  gray characters with complex moral  dilemmas when it comes to our actions as  a player I wouldn't be surprised if  Sebastian's Arc ultimately concludes  with us seeing some of the Slytherin  house traits in a new light another  student who could very well be led to  the dark side is Nat's ionai our  companion from Gryffindor natsai began  her schooling in Africa where she attend  ended wagadu the largest Wizarding  School in the world she moved to  Hogwarts when her mother became the  Divination Professor we also know natsai  is wise quick-witted and possessed of a  need to seek Justice what isn't clear is  if her seeking of justice is part of her  personality or if there's something  deeper in her past that fuels that  desire we get a small glimpse of this in  the cut scene featuring natsai and the  main character this is the one that was  showed during the Autodesk presentation  in this scene it appeared the two were  after some sort of evidence we can  actually hear Nats I say new plan I get  the evidence and you free that  hippogriff agreed this is our chance go  yeah  and of course the big question here how  far will she go in the name of Justice  could it lead her down a dark path now  for our next character the first  impressions are pretty much the complete  opposite of evil poppy Sweeting is  soft-spoken has a love of magical  creatures and belongs to the house  Hufflepuff even her last name is  Sweeting but could Poppy's soft first  impression conceal something much more  Sinister a power that could rival even  the likes of Grindelwald and Voldemort  honestly probably not right and again  there is this the official social media  accounts posted this image of poppy  which looks much older and angrier than  the sweet innocent poppy were introduced  to in the trailer she believes creatures  have far more redeeming qualities than  most people and has a particular  aversion to poachers and those who work  with them so on one hand she seems like  a wonderfully gregarious Hufflepuff in  the vein of Newt scamander but could she  have a darker side darker than Newt  particularly if she Witnesses magical  creatures being harmed and what if those  harming the creatures were someone close  to her such as a fellow student could  she even be tempted to use an  unforgivable curse on them for doing so  evil poppy has essentially become a meme  with the hardcore Hogwarts Legacy fandom  but there's no doubt a young Hufflepuff  girl turning to the dark side would  shock many mainstream players now while  I still don't think it's likely I  certainly would not want to find myself  on Poppy's bad side if you're a fan of  the darker side of the Wizarding World  you'll want to check out the latest  addition to our retro Recon tour item  shop visit retrorecouture.com click  merch and get your unforgivable curses t  or hoodie just in time for Halloween and  after that you can check out my full  breakdown of the Haunted hogsmeade shop  trailer here on the right side of your  screen which absolutely does not shy  away from the horror elements in the  Wizarding World as always thank you all  so much for watching I'll talk to you  again soon
 

